# Project Conventions

## Styling

- Use **Tailwind CSS** and **shadcn/ui** as the preferred methods of styling.
- Avoid inline style objects and raw CSS files unless absolutely necessary.
- Prefer shadcn/ui components over building custom UI primitives.

## Comments & Documentation

- Add a descriptive comment next to **every function** explaining its purpose, parameters, and return value.
- Provide comments and documentation throughout the codebase so that any new contributor can quickly understand the code.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
export function calcTotal(items: CartItem[]) {
  return items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.price * i.qty, 0);
}

// ✅ GOOD
/**
 * Calculates the total price of all items in the cart.
 * @param items - Array of cart items with price and quantity.
 * @returns The summed total price.
 */
export function calcTotal(items: CartItem[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * item.qty, 0);
}
```

## Type Definitions

- All shared TypeScript types and interfaces **must** live in `src/lib/types.ts`.
- Do not define types inline in components; import them from `types.ts`.

## API / Supabase Access

- All Supabase calls and API wrapper functions **must** be defined in `src/lib/api.ts`.
- **Never** call Supabase directly inside components.
- Components should import and call the wrapper functions from `api.ts`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — Supabase called directly in a component
const { data } = await supabase.from("posts").select("*");

// ✅ GOOD — Wrapper in src/lib/api.ts
/** Fetches all posts from the posts table. */
export async function fetchPosts(): Promise<Post[]> {
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from("posts").select("*");
  if (error) throw new Error(error.message);
  return data as Post[];
}

// ✅ GOOD — Component calls the wrapper
import { fetchPosts } from "@/lib/api";
const posts = await fetchPosts();
```

## File Organization Summary

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Shared types & interfaces | `src/lib/types.ts` |
| Supabase / API wrappers | `src/lib/api.ts` |
| Utility helpers | `src/lib/utils.ts` |

always keep website security in mind where applicable